#!RuleTest
#test DRAFT-900044 expect=violation domain=ADSL
#note "RFSTDTC is carried over from DM: the ADaM standard does not define it on ADSL, so the NAME-keyed companion lookup runs. The companion publishes exactly one label for the name and this dataset carries a different one, so the ERROR level fires. || The carry-over operands must be populated into the EVALUATION context (RuleRunner's per-column loop, before evaluateBroadcast) -- populating them only in buildVariableMetadata, which runs after a check has already fired, leaves this scenario silent."
#expectViolationCount 1
#library-include DRAFT-900044-library.yaml
dataset ADSL
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col RFSTDTC type=Char label="First Exposure Date"
---
CDISCPILOT01 | 01-701-1015 | 2026-01-01
---
